¬}\pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 runModalForDirectory:file:types:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (int)\b runModalForDirectory:\b0 (NSString *)\i path \
\fi0 \b \i0 file:\b0 (NSString *)\i name \
\fi0 \b \i0 types:\b0 (NSArray *)\i fileTypes\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Displays the NSOpenPanel and begins its event loop. The NSOpenPanel displays the files in \i path\i0  that match the types in \i fileTypes\i0  (an NSArray of file extensions as NSString objects). If \i path\i0  is \b nil\b0  the directory the application is "currently in" is substituted (on Mach, this is the user\'27s home directory); in later invocations of the shared NSOpenPanel, the directory is by default the last directory where a file was opened, unless specified otherwise with \b setDirectory:\b0 .  If all files and subdirectories should be included in the next column of a browser, \i fileTypes\i0  should be \b nil\b0 . If \i name\i0  specifies a particular file, it is selected when the Open dialog or panel is presented to the user; otherwise, \i name\i0  should be \b nil\b0 . This method returns NSOKButton (if the user clicks the OK button) or NSCancelButton (if the user clicks the Cancel button).\
\fs14\
\pard \s58 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b runModalForTypes:\
